'''Programmer Art''' ({{in|java}}) and the '''Minecraft Classic Texture Pack''' ({{in|bedrock|ps4}}) are [[resource pack]]s that primarily use classic ''Minecraft'' [[textures]] from before the [[Texture Update]]. The name in ''Java Edition'' refers to the fact that these textures were created by the programmers of the game, rather than a dedicated art team; the term [[w:programmer art|programmer art]] is common for referring to such assets in video games.

The equivalent resource packs are built into ''Java Edition'' and ''PlayStation 4 Edition'', and available as a free download on the [[Marketplace]] in ''Bedrock Edition''.

